<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria M1 falls 0.57 pct, M2 up 1.25 pct in week.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria M1 falls 0.57 pct, M2 up 1.25 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian M1 money supply fell to 889 billion levs on June 27 from 894.1 billion levs a week earlier, while M2 increased to 3,801.4 billion levs from 3,754.4 billion, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Total broad money rose 1.18 percent to 4,018.1 billion levs in the week to June 27.</p>
<p>Conversion of dollar-denominated deposits into levs was made at the central bank fixings of 1,711.6 levs per dollar on June 27, 1,697.3 for June 20 and 1,568.1 for May 30.</p>
